inding":"The plan makes 'the committed FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS value' load-bearing for step 3 and AC-4 but never states what that value is; the docker bridge gateway peer IP is network-dependent and can drift, so a naively-chosen fixed IP would silently re-open the http:// downgrade while the local ASGI test still passes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a295af82bf07b2e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 + AC-4 (FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS)","norm_id":"ncc969cffc1365ce0","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer picks a specific bridge-gateway IP that later changes across a docker network recreate; ProxyHeadersMiddleware stops trusting the peer; absolute URLs regress to http:// while the in-process test (which supplies its own trusted peer) still passes"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Commit FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=\"*\" on the mcp service and note the existing rationale (host-loopback publish + nginx overwriting X-Forwarded-Proto as a literal) makes trust-all safe here; have the compose structural test assert the exact committed value.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm against the installed uvicorn source that a programmatically-built uvicorn.Config honors FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS from the environment (and enables proxy_headers by default); if not, amend step 3 to pass forwarded_allow_ips explicitly to the Config at _mcp_health.py:311-317 rather than relying on 'no code change'.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Set FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS on the mcp compose service so uvicorn's ProxyHeadersMiddleware trusts nginx's forwarded proto. No code change is needed (uvicorn reads the variable natively)'","resolve_symbol: uvicorn.middleware.proxy_headers.ProxyHeadersMiddleware EXISTS; uvicorn.config.Config EXISTS (Partially-verified — the env-var-native defaulting for a non-CLI Config was not observable, venv outside snapshot)","_mcp_health.py:311-317 constructs uvicorn.Config directly with no forwarded_allow_ips and no explicit proxy_headers flag","Mitigation present: Testing tier adds an in-process ASGI test through ProxyHeadersMiddleware configured from the committed compose value, serving as an executable oracle"],"finding":"Step 3 asserts uvicorn reads FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS 'natively' and needs 'No code change' — but the app builds uvicorn.Config programmatically (src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:311-317), not via the uvicorn CLI. Whether a programmatically-constructed Config honors the FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS env var (and wires ProxyHeadersMiddleware with proxy_headers enabled) is a load-bearing, version-dependent behavior the plan does not verify against the installed uvicorn source; resolve_symbol confirms the middleware/Config classes exist but not the env-var defaulting path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc168174056f57c2e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:311-317","norm_id":"nf488ac3b49b23d3f","priority":0.65,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A uvicorn version where programmatic Config does not read FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS from the environment (or defaults proxy_headers off) would leave scheme derivation as http:// despite the compose env var being set"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS value to commit (e.g. the docker bridge subnet CIDR, or a documented rationale for '*' given the loopback-only publish) so the trust peer is a decision, not an executor guess.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 3: 'Set FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS on the mcp compose service so uvicorn's ProxyHeadersMiddleware trusts nginx's forwarded proto' — value unstated","AC: 'With the committed FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS value in force ... plus a structural assertion that FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS is set on the compose mcp service' — asserts presence, not the correct value","RCA notes nginx's connection arrives from the docker bridge gateway, which is not necessarily a fixed IP across environments"],"finding":"The plan repeatedly relies on 'the committed FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS value' but never states what that value should be (docker bridge gateway IP, the bridge subnet CIDR, or '*'), leaving the actual trust-peer selection as a design choice deferred to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb3b1c18e67abe14a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / Acceptance Criteria (FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS)","norm_id":"n0d02ca50a4a3be54","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor sets a value that doesn't match the actual docker bridge peer, so X-Forwarded-Proto is still dropped in production while the in-process test (configured from that same value with a synthetic peer) passes green"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Specify the value in Step 3 — e.g. FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS set to the docker bridge subnet/gateway used by the mcp service, or '*' justified by the fact that the port is published only on host loopback with nginx as the sole reachable client (as the plan already argues in Step 3's spoofing note).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attribut